# Launch readiness (pre-Amazon)

Studio **export ≠ live on Amazon**. AuthorForge and NovelForge must keep a **Launch readiness** checklist on the Publish step covering:

1. Manuscript & product quality (edit pass; AF story slots/facts; NF continuity/adult content)
2. Amazon / KDP account (tax, marketplace language, pricing, ISBN, categories, AI disclosure, Previewer, barcode zone)
3. Studio setup (live LLM, desktop/credits, backup, trim/paper verify)
4. After export (manual KDP upload, Look Inside, optional A+, post-publish updates)
5. Strategy (niche tips are guidance, not sales data)

Canonical data: `LAUNCH_READINESS` + helpers in each studio’s `publishing-specs.js`.  
UI: `LaunchReadinessPanel` on Publish. Persist ticks on `book.compliance.checklist`.  
Specs: `GET /v1/specs` includes `launch_readiness: launchReadinessPayload()`.

Do **not** reintroduce a one-click “Mark compliance reviewed” that skips the phased checklist.  
Do **not** claim the app uploads to Amazon or certifies KDP acceptance.
